# Project-root .vercelignore for the Next.js app.
#
# Vercel's monorepo behavior: when the project root directory (frontend/)
# contains its own .vercelignore, it takes precedence over the one at the
# repository root. Without this file, the repo-root .vercelignore (written for
# the Python backend, which ignores src/) is applied here too — and since those
# are gitignore-style unanchored patterns, `src/` matched frontend/src/ and the
# entire Next.js app source was stripped from uploads, yielding a build with no
# routes (only the platform /404). node_modules and .next are excluded by
# Vercel's defaults, so nothing else needs to be listed.
.next
node_modules
